§ `ss 83A-33, 83A-35, 83A-45`

-- c072, d04b: Chloe joins Jarrah on 2034-02-01 (registered 2031-03-15; about 2 years before its last year end). A
-- hypothetical 10% discount qualifies; 20% does not; nor does a company incorporated 12 years. The discount is then not assessable.
-- A listed employer's broad scheme: 3,000 less the $1,000 reduction of s 83A-35 = 2,000 (income 110,000, under $180,000).
#ASSERT `Do my ESS interests get the start-up concession` `Chloe's Jarrah shares (c072, d04b)`
#ASSERT NOT `Do my ESS interests get the start-up concession` `the same shares at a 20 percent discount`
#ASSERT NOT `Do my ESS interests get the start-up concession` `shares in a company incorporated 12 years`

#ASSERT `How much of my ESS discount is assessable` `Chloe's Jarrah shares (c072, d04b)` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of my ESS discount is assessable` `shares in a listed employer at a 3000 discount` EQUALS 2000

§ `s 83A-30`

-- c085: when Chloe's start-up shares are bought out in 2050, her gain is measured from their market value at acquisition
-- (10,000), not the 9,000 she paid.
#ASSERT `What am I taken to have paid for my ESS interest` `Chloe's Jarrah shares (c072, d04b)` 9000 EQUALS 10000

§ `s 355-100`

-- d049: Jarrah, turnover under $20 million; corporate tax rate 25% (Rates Act s 23(2), base rate entity): 25 + 18.5 = 43.5%,
-- refundable. 100,000 of notional deductions (hypothetical) give 43,500.
#ASSERT `What is my company's R&D offset rate` 5000000 FALSE 25 EQUALS 43.5

#ASSERT `Is my company's R&D offset refundable` 5000000 FALSE

#ASSERT `What R&D offset does my small company get` 100000 0 5000000 25 EQUALS 43500

§ `ss 360-15, 360-20, 360-25`

-- d081: Daniel, a sophisticated investor (amounts hypothetical). 20% of 500,000 = 100,000; 20% of 1,500,000 capped at
-- 200,000. A retail investor paying more than $50,000 in the year gets nothing.
#ASSERT `What early stage investor tax offset do I get` TRUE TRUE 500000 0 EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `What early stage investor tax offset do I get` TRUE TRUE 1500000 0 EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `What early stage investor tax offset do I get` TRUE FALSE 60000 0 EQUALS 0

